From: mscharged-port
Subject: Append DWC's added match filter without an overlapping snprintf
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native libc compatibility

DWCi_SBUpdateAsync adds the game's filter to the default match filter
with snprintf(filter, sizeof(filter), "%s and (%s)", filter, ...), whose
source overlaps its destination. CodeWarrior's formatter read the source
before overwriting it; glibc does not, so the default part was lost and
the server browser received " and (AP = ... and CO = 0)", which the
server rejected: "Error parsing filter: unexpected end of expression".

Natively the added filter is appended after the default one, producing
the same string, truncation included.

diff --git a/src/RVL_SDK/dwc/dwc_match.c b/src/RVL_SDK/dwc/dwc_match.c
index b8c5085..86678c6 100644
--- a/src/RVL_SDK/dwc/dwc_match.c
+++ b/src/RVL_SDK/dwc/dwc_match.c
@@ -2258,8 +2258,19 @@ static SBError DWCi_SBUpdateAsync(int profileID)
 
             if (stpAddFilter)
             {
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_NATIVE)
+                // The original formats filter into itself. glibc does not
+                // read an overlapping source, so the default filter was lost;
+                // append the game's filter after it instead.
+                {
+                    size_t used = strlen(filter);
+                    (void)snprintf(filter + used, sizeof(filter) - used,
+                        " and (%s)", stpAddFilter);
+                }
+#else
                 (void)snprintf(filter, sizeof(filter), "%s and (%s)", filter,
                     stpAddFilter);
+#endif
             }
             break;
         }
